{"absent":["Lock rules: fragments show no locks, shared-state protection or ordering requirements.","State machines: no lifecycle, phase or transition model is visible beyond the enabled-gated user-enter request.","Selection conditions choosing alt_1 versus alt_2 spellings, including compiler versions and configuration symbols, are not shown.","Definitions of container_of, the context-tracking key and user state value, and sanitizer and tracing primitives referenced by the markers are not shown.","Numeric ABI values, structure offsets, alignment guarantees and calling conventions are not shown.","Error handling, return values and concurrency effects of the user-enter path beyond the enabled gate are not shown."],"dossier":"D17","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__always_inline","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__gnu_inline","include/linux/compiler_types.h::inline","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__inline__","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__inline_maybe_unused.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__inline_maybe_unused.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::noinline","include/linux/compiler_types.h::noinline_for_stack","include/linux/compiler_types.h::noinline_for_tracing","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__flatten","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noclone.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noclone.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noipa.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noipa.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__cold.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__cold.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__naked","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__weak","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__alias","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__function_aligned.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__function_aligned.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_caller_saved_registers.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_caller_saved_registers.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__fix_address","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noreturn"],"text":"Portable function and linkage controls abstract compiler-specific code generation choices. The group covers forced inlining and GNU inline semantics, suppression of inlining including stack and tracing variants, flattening, clone suppression, interprocedural-analysis suppression, cold marking, naked functions, weak linkage, symbol aliasing, externally visible linkage, function alignment selection, caller-saved-register suppression, non-returning marking, and a helper that pins an address by combining noinline with noclone. An inline wrapper also composes GNU inline with unused handling and tracing exclusion."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__aligned","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__aligned_largest","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__packed","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__mode","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__section","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__always_unused","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__maybe_unused","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__used","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__always_used","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__retain.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__retain.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_ptr.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_ptr.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_le.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_be.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_le.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by_be.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__nonstring.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__nonstring.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nonstring_array.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nonstring_array.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__uninitialized.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__uninitialized.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__cleanup","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__randomize_layout.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_randomize_layout.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::randomized_struct_fields_start.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::randomized_struct_fields_end.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__randomize_layout.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_randomize_layout.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::randomized_struct_fields_start.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::randomized_struct_fields_end.alt_2"],"text":"Portable type, layout and lifetime markers abstract alignment, packing, machine mode, section placement, retention and flexible-array bounds. The set includes requested and largest alignment, packed layout, mode selection, section naming, used and unused markers with an always-used combination, retain marking, counted-by and pointer-counted-by bounds with little-endian and big-endian selected forms, nonstring and nonstring-array markers, uninitialized marking, scoped cleanup attachment, and structure randomization controls with start and end helpers plus opt-out marking."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__printf","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__scanf","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__nonnull_args","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__must_check","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pure","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__attribute_const__","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__malloc","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__alloc_size__","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__alloc_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__realloc_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__alloc_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__realloc_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_object_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_object_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_dynamic_object_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_dynamic_object_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__assume_aligned","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__assume.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__assume.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__copy.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__copy.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__overloadable.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__overloadable.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__diagnose_as.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__diagnose_as.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__designated_init.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__designated_init.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_error.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_error.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_warning.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_warning.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__annotated","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__deprecated"],"text":"Portable contract and diagnostic markers declare checking intent for functions and variables. Coverage includes printf-like and scanf-like format checking, null-argument checking, unused-result checking, purity and constness, malloc-like allocation sizing with realloc sizing, dynamic and static object-size passing, assumed alignment and assumed values, attribute copying, overloadable marking, builtin diagnosis, designated-initializer enforcement, compile-time error and warning reporting, attribute presence query, and a deprecated marker that carries no effect in the routed configuration."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noclone.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__noclone.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_stack_protector.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_stack_protector.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__cold.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__cold.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__preserve_most.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__preserve_most.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__retain.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__retain.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__counted_by.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__assume.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__assume.alt_2"],"text":"Many macros use paired alternatives where one form carries a compiler capability and the other degrades to empty or to a benign default. The invariant is that the name always exists so callers need no conditionals, and unsupported toolchains lose only the extra optimization, checking or diagnostic effect. This pattern applies across visibility, cloning, profiling, stack protection, sanitizer, cold, preserve-most, retain, counted-by, assumption and diagnostic helpers."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::ftrace_branch_data","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ftrace_branch_data.anon_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ftrace_branch_data.anon_1.anon_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ftrace_branch_data.anon_1.anon_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ftrace_likely_data"],"text":"Branch profile state uses a base record holding function name, file name and line number plus a union with three views: correct with incorrect counts, miss with hit counts, and a two-element array. A second structure wraps one base record and adds a constant field for likely or unlikely annotation sites."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::__kernel.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__user.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__iomem.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__percpu.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__rcu.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__chk_user_ptr.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__chk_io_ptr.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__force.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocast.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__safe.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__private.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ACCESS_PRIVATE.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__kernel.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__user.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__user.alt_3","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__iomem.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__percpu.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__rcu.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__chk_user_ptr.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__chk_io_ptr.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__force.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocast.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__safe.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__private.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ACCESS_PRIVATE.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::BTF_TYPE_TAG.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::BTF_TYPE_TAG.alt_2"],"text":"Static-checker pointer annotations separate kernel, user, input-output memory, per-cpu and read-copy-update pointer kinds, with force, nocast, safe and private qualifiers and a helper for accessing private members. Small validation helpers for user and input-output pointers perform a check in the checking configuration and become no-ops otherwise. Optional type tags and compiler user attributes provide alternate spellings for the same separation when the checker is absent."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::notrace.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::notrace.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::notrace.alt_3","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_kasan_or_inline.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_sanitize_or_inline.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_kasan_or_inline.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_kcsan.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_sanitize_or_inline.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_kcsan.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_sanitize_or_inline.alt_3","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_sanitize_or_inline.alt_4","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__disable_sanitizer_instrumentation.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__disable_sanitizer_instrumentation.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__no_kstack_erase","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__noscs","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocfi.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocfi.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocfi_generic.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__nocfi_generic.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__preserve_most.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__preserve_most.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__noinstr_section","include/linux/compiler_types.h::noinstr","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__cpuidle"],"text":"Tracing, profiling, sanitizer and integrity exclusions mark code that must run without instrumentation. The family includes three notrace spellings, kasan and kcsan exclusion with a combined no-sanitize-or-inline selector across kasan, kcsan and kmsan configurations, sanitizer-instrumentation disabling, profiling exclusion, stack-erase and shadow-call-stack exclusions, control-flow-integrity exclusions, preserve-most marking, and section-based no-instrumentation markers for generic noinstr code and for cpuidle code."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::__compiletime_assert.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__compiletime_assert.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::_compiletime_assert","include/linux/compiler_types.h::compiletime_assert","include/linux/compiler_types.h::compiletime_assert_atomic_type","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__native_word","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__same_type","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__scalar_type_to_expr_cases","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__unqual_scalar_typeof.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__unqual_scalar_typeof.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__scalar_type_to_signed_cases","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__signed_scalar_typeof","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__struct_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__member_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__struct_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__member_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__flex_counter.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__flex_counter.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__has_builtin","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__builtin_warning"],"text":"Compile-time assertion and type introspection helpers support static validation and qualifier-insensitive scalar handling. Facilities include a generic assertion with counter-based unique naming, an atomic-type width check requiring native-word-sized access, a native-word predicate, same-type comparison, unqualified and signed scalar type selection across standard integer kinds, structure-size and member-size queries with dynamic and static variants, a flexible-array counter accessor with null fallback, a builtin-presence constant, and a builtin-warning constant."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::___PASTE","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__PASTE","include/linux/compiler_types.h::auto","include/linux/compiler_types.h::asm_goto_output","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_INPUT_G","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_INPUT_RM","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_OUTPUT_RM","include/linux/compiler_types.h::asm_inline.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::asm_inline.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__data_racy.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__data_racy.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__latent_entropy","include/linux/compiler_types.h::at_least.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_types.h::at_least.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::USE_TYPEOF_UNQUAL","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_GCC","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_clang","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_push","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_pop","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_ignore","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_warn","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_error","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__diag_ignore_all"],"text":"Preprocessor, assembly and diagnostic utilities provide token pasting, a short automatic-type name, volatile assembly goto output, assembly operand markers, an assembly-inline selector, a data-racy marker, a latent-entropy marker, an array-bound marker with static and empty forms, a type-unqualification selector, and a diagnostic push, pop and severity family that degrades to empty in the routed configuration."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/container_of.h::typeof_member","include/linux/container_of.h::container_of_const","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__LINUX_COMPILER_ATTRIBUTES_H","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__LINUX_COMPILER_TYPES_H","include/linux/const.h::_LINUX_CONST_H","include/linux/container_of.h::_LINUX_CONTAINER_OF_H","include/linux/context_tracking.h::_LINUX_CONTEXT_TRACKING_H"],"text":"Container and header-identity helpers expose member-type extraction and a const-preserving container lookup that yields a const-qualified result for const inputs and a mutable result otherwise. Include guards identify the compiler-attribute, compiler-type, constant, container and context-tracking headers."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/context_tracking.h::user_enter.alt_1","include/linux/context_tracking_state.h::context_tracking_enabled.alt_1"],"text":"User entry observes whether context tracking is enabled and only then requests transition to user state. The enabled query is an always-inline boolean check backed by a static-branch predicate owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__deprecated","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_object_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_object_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_dynamic_object_size.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__pass_dynamic_object_size.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_stack_protector.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_stack_protector.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_profile.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::fallthrough.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::fallthrough.alt_2"],"text":"Several fallbacks silently drop safety effects and must not be relied on for diagnostics or protection. The deprecated marker is empty, object-size passing and several sanitizer and protection exclusions can vanish, and the switch fallthrough helper has two shapes where one needs compiler support and the other is an empty loop needing statement context."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_INPUT_G","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_INPUT_RM","include/linux/compiler_types.h::ASM_OUTPUT_RM"],"text":"Inline assembly operand markers use short conventional codes distinguishing a generic input from read-allow and read-write memory operands, with separate spellings for the generic input form, the read-allow input form and the read-write output form."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_unlikely.alt_1"],"text":"External static-branch query owned by another dossier and relied on by the context-tracking enabled check."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/jump_label.h::static_branch_unlikely.alt_2"],"text":"Alternate form of the external static-branch query owned by another dossier and relied on by the context-tracking enabled check."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":38,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"927ee632d14b551f83fe7a9f162d15595fedc350d6bff7bdce52995e491e86d4","prompt_sha256":"4a998154259ec174b8eca0183a6755847c856ec1e800fc8e006bcf5bc9af1b4b","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__LINUX_COMPILER_ATTRIBUTES_H","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__alias","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__aligned","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__aligned_largest","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__alloc_size__","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__always_inline","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__assume_aligned","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__cleanup","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__attribute_const__","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__copy.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__copy.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__diagnose_as.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__diagnose_as.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__deprecated","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__designated_init.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__designated_init.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_error.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__compiletime_error.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_1","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__visible.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__printf","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__scanf","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__gnu_inline","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__malloc","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__mode","include/linux/compiler_attributes.h::__no_caller_saved_registers.al